Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC25)
Why this approach: fixtureIdentifiers walks the module like go test ./... (skipping "." and "_" directories and nested modules), scans each file with a testdata directory among its parents line by line, and reports file:line: rule for each match of a fixed rule list (sk-ant-, bearer + token in any case, UUID, email, wrkspc_, and organization / account_uuid / org_id case-insensitively). The scanner is a plain function, so TestFixtureScanner_FlagsEachIdentifier proves it on a seeded temp module.
Alternatives rejected: whole-word matching for the banned names (would miss Anthropic-Organization-Id style headers); only scanning internal/protocols/anthropic/testdata (the task asks for every testdata directory).
Trade-off / known limit: the rules are case-insensitive substrings, so prose such as "organizations" in a fixture README would also fail; "Bearer" alone with no following token is allowed. Hidden and underscore directories and nested modules are not scanned.
Verified by: TestFixtures_NoIdentifiers passes over the committed golden fixture; proved by appending an Anthropic-Organization-Id UUID header to stream.headers (flagged as uuid and organization) and by disabling the match (seeded test failed with nothing found), both reverted; make verify.
